摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"English · 简体中文","id":"gh:1421471999","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-task-ledger","slug":"cq-guojia/dsh-task-ledger","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"# dsh-task-ledger"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**English** · 简体中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Task tracking for AI coding agents. A task is opened, claimed, advanced and closed by the agent itse"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"lf, and every one of those steps is written into a plain-text `ledger/` directory inside the reposit"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"ory — so the owner of a task, its current state, the next step and the conclusion remain on record i"},{"id":"p3s4","text":"nstead of dissolving into chat history."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## Why it exists"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Work that spans several sessions, several days or several people loses three answers: who is doing i"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"t, how far it has progressed, and what it was supposed to achieve. A chat log does not preserve them"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" reliably, and a hosted project tool keeps them outside the repository, away from the code they desc"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ably, and a hosted project tool keeps them outside the repository, away from the code they describe."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"This ledger keeps those answers next to the code, in files that can be read, diffed and reviewed. Fo"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ur properties define it:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"| Property | What it means |"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| **Task lifecycle tracking** | Tasks are created, claimed, resumed, handed over and closed. Every t"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ransition carries a timestamp and an owner; free-form progress, the conclusion and open issues live "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"in the task document. |\n| **Local by design** | No account, no hosted backend, no service marketplac"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"e. The ledger is plain JSON and Markdown committed with the repository; it works offline and is revi"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"ewable in a pull request. |\n| **Single-user and multi-user** | One person on one machine, or a team "},{"id":"p8s6","text":"sharing one repository. Ownership state is sharded per person, so two people advancing two tasks nev"},{"id":"p8s7","text":"er write the same file. |\n| **Version control as the sync layer** | Git is the transport. Push, pull"},{"id":"p8s8","text":" and merge carry the ledger between machines and contributors, and commit history doubles as the aud"},{"id":"p8s9","text":"carry the ledger between machines and contributors, and commit history doubles as the audit trail. |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Two packages"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"This repository ships one capability in two forms. They share a single source of truth for the skill"},{"id":"p10s2","text":", so the two never drift apart."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Package | Form | Who it is for | Install |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| `dsh-task-ledger` | Plugin for DeepSeek Harness: full board UI, with the skill bundled | dsh users"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" | `dsh plugin add dsh-task-ledger` |\n| `task-ledger` | Standalone skill: instructions, CLI and asse"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"ts only | Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, CodeBuddy, WorkBuddy, Trae, and any other agent that loads `SK"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ILL.md` | see below |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Detailed documentation lives in each package: plugin · skill."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Installing the skill in an agent"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### With a skill manager"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"The skills CLI (Vercel) writes the skill into every agent it detects and keeps it updated:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The path matters: this repository holds two copies of the skill, and pointing at `packages/skill` se"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"lects the source. Add `-g` to install for all projects instead of the current one."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"SkillHub and the markets built into CodeBuddy and WorkBuddy install a skill once it is listed; when "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"search does not find `task-ledger`, use the client's local import and point it at `packages/skill`, "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"or add this repository as a GitHub source."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Manually"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The skill is a directory containing `SKILL.md` and a prebuilt CLI. Installing it means copying that "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"directory into the skills directory of the agent you use. Fetch the source once:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Then copy it to the location your agent reads. User-level paths apply to every project; project-leve"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"l paths apply to one repository and are committed, which is how a team shares the same skill."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| Agent | User-level directory | Command |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| Claude Code | `~/.claude/skills/` | `mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills && cp -R /tmp/task-ledger-src/packa"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ges/skill ~/.claude/skills/task-ledger` |\n| Cursor | `~/.cursor/skills/` | `mkdir -p ~/.cursor/skill"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"s && cp -R /tmp/task-ledger-src/packages/skill ~/.cursor/skills/task-ledger` |\n| Codex CLI | `~/.cod"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"ex/skills/` | `mkdir -p ~/.codex/skills && cp -R /tmp/task-ledger-src/packages/skill ~/.codex/skills"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"/task-ledger` |\n| CodeBuddy | `~/.codebuddy/skills/` | `mkdir -p ~/.codebuddy/skills && cp -R /tmp/t"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"ask-ledger-src/packages/skill ~/.codebuddy/skills/task-ledger` |\n| WorkBuddy | `~/.workbuddy/skills/"},{"id":"p25s7","text":"` | `mkdir -p ~/.workbuddy/skills && cp -R /tmp/task-ledger-src/packages/skill ~/.workbuddy/skills/t"},{"id":"p25s8","text":"ask-ledger` |\n| Trae | `~/.trae/skills/` (Trae CN: `~/.trae-cn/skills/`) | `mkdir -p ~/.trae/skills "},{"id":"p25s9","text":"&& cp -R /tmp/task-ledger-src/packages/skill ~/.trae/skills/task-ledger` |"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Notes:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- **Project-level install** — the same copies work under the repository: `.claude/skills/`, `.cursor"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"/skills/`, `.codebuddy/skills/`, `.trae/skills/`, or `.agents/skills/` for the cross-agent conventio"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"n read by Codex and Cursor.\n- **Doubao Work (豆包工作)** — import the folder from the application: open "},{"id":"p27s4","text":"the sidebar, choose Skills, and import `packages/skill` as a local skill.\n- **Windows** — substitute"},{"id":"p27s5","text":" `%USERPROFILE%\\` for `~`. Everywhere below, replace `scripts/progress` with `scripts\\bin\\ledger-win"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"dows-amd64.exe`: CreateProcessW cannot execute an extensionless sh wrapper (it appends `.exe`, finds"},{"id":"p27s7","text":" nothing, and fails). The wrapper still works under Git Bash / WSL.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Using it"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"There are no commands for you to type. The ledger is driven by what you say to the agent: when a req"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"uest matches one of the intents below, the agent runs the corresponding operation and records it."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| You say | What the agent does | Result |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| \"Open a task: get the release pipeline working\" | creates the task with the tags you gave | In the"},{"id":"p31s2","text":" shared pool, state `open`, unclaimed |\n| \"Open a task and start on it\" | creates and claims it | Ow"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"ned by you, state `doing` |\n| \"I'll take that one\" / \"continue with X\" | claims the task | Moved to "},{"id":"p31s4","text":"your name, state `doing` |\n| *(while working)* | writes the task document, then appends an execution"},{"id":"p31s5","text":" record | Progress, conclusions and blockers on record |\n| \"Blocked for now\" / \"leave it for a while"},{"id":"p31s6","text":"\" | records the blocker, leaves the state alone | Still `doing` — a pause is neither a release nor a"},{"id":"p31s7","text":" cancellation |\n| \"Hand it back\" | releases it | Returns to the shared pool for anyone to claim |\n| "},{"id":"p31s8","text":"\"Close this task\" | closes it with your summary | One row written to history; read-only afterwards |"},{"id":"p31s9","text":"\n| \"Cancel it\" | closes it as void, with the reason | Closed, not completed |\n| \"Delete it\" | asks y"},{"id":"p31s10","text":"ou to confirm, then deletes | Removed permanently — no undo, no restore |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## What gets written"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"State and prose are kept apart: JSON holds who owns what and in which state, Markdown holds the reas"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"oning. Only the CLI writes state, history and the execution log; the agent writes the first five sec"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"tions of a task document and nothing else."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
